# Taskmark project memory

If a Taskmark board exists in the workspace, treat it as the source of truth for planned, in-flight, and done product work.

1. **Board location:**
   - **Single git project:** board at `<project>/taskmark/` (uses that project’s git).
   - **Multiple git projects:** dedicated sibling `<common_project_name>-taskmark` whose **repo root is the board** (`INDEX.md`, `epics/` at the root — never `<name>-taskmark/taskmark/`). Own git. Never copy the board into product repos. If the common name is ambiguous, ask the user.
   - Run `sync-taskmark-repos` at session start / after board layout changes to refresh `REPOS.md` (and migrate leftovers with `--migrate` when needed).
2. Before implementing a feature, bug fix, or product refactor: search the board for a matching epic/story/task/bug and **link work to it**.
3. If none exists and the work is real product scope, **create** items (`create-epic` / `create-story` / `create-task`) — no orphan product changes without a board trail.
4. When planning a new iteration, read `INDEX.md`, `VELOCITY.md`, **Prompt & feedback** logs, and **Commits** so prior decisions, sizes/points, and shipped work carry forward.
5. On each user turn tied to an item: append prompt/feedback, manage Work log (`start-work` / `complete-work`), **log commits** for touched repos, then implement; run `sync-status` after AC or session changes (idle-caps abandoned sessions; runs `recompute-actuals.py --calibrate`). When asking about speed/ETA, use `taskmark-velocity`. When committing across projects, use `commit-all`.
6. Never invent a parallel todo list in chat; update markdown under the **canonical board root** only.
7. Never treat calendar span as **Actual**. Actual = billable Work log minutes (script-derived). Never hand-set `actual_minutes` / `effort_minutes`. When one sitting delivers many leaves, **split** batch minutes by points (shared-batch) — never copy the full Started/Ended onto every task. Always recompute via the script on complete/sync.
